--- !u!114 &1383125439
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1383125437}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<color=#45A8FF><b>COCKPIT CONTROLS</b></color>

    <b>Look around</b>   hold the right mouse button and move the mouse

    <b>Jump to a view</b>   1 window   2 displays   3 main panel   4 left console   5 right console   6 overhead

    <b>Zoom</b>   hold Z or the middle mouse button


    <b>Buttons</b>   point and left-click. Red-framed buttons are guarded: the first click lifts the guard, the second presses.

    <b>Switches</b>   left-click to flip. The lamp above shows the state.

    <b>Dials</b>   hold left-click and drag, or point and scroll the wheel.

    <b>Throttle</b>   drag the lever on the left console, scroll over it, or use Shift and Ctrl. T is full, X is idle.

    <b>Attitude</b>   W S pitch, A D yaw, Q E roll (guidance off, RCS on).


    <color=#45A8FF><b>THE THREE DISPLAYS</b></color>

    <b>Left</b>   flight and navigation: altitude, velocity, attitude, trajectory.

    <b>Centre</b>   systems: engine, fuel, power, cabin, launch status and alerts.

    <b>Right</b>   hull camera, current objective and the flight-event timeline.


    The control you need next pulses amber, and the objective is shown top left. Esc pauses.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
